In an online Entertainment Tonight special posted the same day that the series conclusion premiered on Disney+ , Gomez looks back on how far she&#8217;s come since she first made her debut as Alex on the original Disney Channel series in 2007. After running for four seasons, Wizards of Waverly Place wrapped in 2012 &#8212; more than a decade after which the Rare Beauty founder and costar David Henrie teamed up to resurrect the show for a reboot.

&#8220;This is it. This is the end,&#8221; Gomez said between previews of scenes from the Wizards Beyond Waverly Place finale and behind-the-scenes footage of the cast hugging and laughing on set. &#8220;It&#8217;s really surreal to say that I&#8217;m done playing this character.&#8221;

&#8220;My hope is that people fall in love with family shows again, and that they hold this to a standard of appreciating what it means to just have a show that the whole family can get together, watch, hopefully laugh,&#8221; she continued. &#8220;I&#8217;m going to really miss that.&#8221;

In addition to reprising her role as Alex, the Only Murders in the Building star made her directorial debut on the third and final installment of Wizards Beyond Waverly Place . The emotional conclusion brings back one of the original show&#8217;s most beloved characters: Harper Finkle, played by Jennifer Stone, who returned for the finale after being absent from the spin-off&#8217;s first two seasons.

&#8220;Filming with Selena, I was a mess,&#8221; Stone told ET . &#8220;It felt like saying goodbye to, in a weird way, your teenage self.&#8221;

After rising to superstardom in the 2010s on the original Wizards of Waverly Place , Gomez forged a successful career as a pop star. She&#8217;s notched 46 songs on the Billboard Hot 100 &#8212; including No. 1 smash &#8220;Lose You to Love Me&#8221; in 2019 &#8212; and most recently dropped music at the end of July, new single single &#8220;Te Olvido (La La),&#8221; which is a collaboration with husband Benny Blanco and Becky G.

